<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>5.2.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01253</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.2.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>2dbcead3-af69-4557-8344-5ab413474ff5</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para><emphasis><emphasis>Students will complete the following questions to practice the skills they have learned in this lesson.</emphasis></emphasis></para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>
    Simplify \(\sqrt[4]{81}\).
  </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 3</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>
    Simplify \(\sqrt[5]{-32}\).
  </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> –2</para>
<para>3. Which of the following is equivalent to \(\sqrt[4]{x^3}\)?</para>
<list>
  <item>
    \(x^\frac34\)
  </item>
  <item>
    \(x^\frac43\)
  </item>
  <item>
    \(4x^3\)
  </item>
  <item>
    \(\frac34x\)
  </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x^\frac34\)</para>
<para>4. Which of the following is equivalent to \(\sqrt[9]{2^4}\)?</para>
<list>
  <item>
    \(2^\frac94\)
  </item>
  <item>
    \(\frac49(2)\)
  </item>
  <item>
    \(\frac{2^4}9\)
  </item>
  <item>
    \(2^\frac49\)
  </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(2^\frac49\)</para>
<para>5. Simplify \(k^3\;\cdot\;k^\frac13\).</para>
<list>
  <item>\(k\)</item>
  <item>
    \(\frac13k^3\)
  </item>
  <item>
    \(3k^\frac13\)
  </item>
  <item>
    \(k^\frac{10}3\)
  </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(k^\frac{10}3\)</para>
<para>6. Simplify \({(m^\frac34)}^{-2}\).</para>
<list>
  <item>
    \(m^\frac68\)
  </item>
  <item>
    \(\frac1{m^\frac32}\)
  </item>
  <item>
    \(m^\frac32\)
  </item>
  <item>
    \(-2m^\frac34\)
  </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(\frac1{m^\frac32}\)</para>
<para>7. True or false:</para>
<para>\(\sqrt[4]{-16}\;=\;-2\)</para>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> False</para>
<para>8. True or false:</para>
<para>\(\sqrt[3]{-64}\;=\;-4\)</para>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> True</para>
<para>9. Which of the following expressions are equivalent to perfect squares? <emphasis>Select the three</emphasis> that apply.</para>
<list>
  <item>
    25
  </item>
  <item>
    \(\sqrt{16}\)
  </item>
  <item>
    \(3+3\)
  </item>
  <item>
    \(\sqrt[5]{9^5}\)
  </item>
  <item>
    \(3\;\cdot\;2\)
  </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 25, \(\sqrt{16}\), \(\sqrt[5]{9^5}\)</para>
<para>10. Which of the following is equivalent to \({(x^\frac15)}^4\)?</para>
<list>
  <item>
    \(x^4\)
  </item>
  <item>
    \(x^\frac45\)
  </item>
  <item>
    \(x^\frac4{20}\)
  </item>
  <item>
    \(x^{20}\)
  </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x^\frac45\)</para></section>
</content>
